  "reason": "Existing evidence shows scvi_n200 (best RNA encoder) achieves 0.65 accuracy in multiprofile, while image-only models (e.g., resnet50) are weak (0.207). Testing multimodal with scvi_n200 and ViT (a stronger image encoder) in singleprofile isolates the impact of combining modalities. This addresses uncertainty about whether multimodal approaches can outperform RNA-only baselines, leveraging the best RNA encoder with a superior image encoder to test a key design choice efficiently."
